it's a journey that still haunts him why  did the others die she could do wonders  and why did he survive on board were  friends and neighbors from barra all  hoping to make it to Europe he says they  had meticulously planned the trip for  weeks but the ocean often brings the  unexpected running out of fuel in food  they had decided to turn around for  supplies when a wave hit them people  panicked the boat capsized off the coast  of Mauritania [ __ ] friends died while he  swam to shore I pray that they have  forgiven me and I hope that I can one  day complete their journey so that we  can all find some peace among the dead  Sofia to a 16 year old orphan Tita Gomez  died with her six-year-old son in her  arms and Jojo Bujang these were young  Gambians fleeing not war but the poverty  in their country  Georgia worked as a waitress in a bar  catering to tourists from Gambia Europe  seems so close at home she would ask her  aunt why it's so easy for Europeans to  come to Africa and so hard for Africans  to go to Europe don't you know for a  better life and to help his parents and  the family that's all he went to the sea  she paid $700 to travel from Barra  to the Canary Islands by boat while the  trafficker who arranged this trip is in  hiding there is no shortage of boatman  willing to make the journey  these are boats made for fishing not to  transport people through the Atlantic  Ocean to the shores of Europe and yet  migrants pack in these vessels sleeping  here eating here sometimes they get lost  on the way so the journey can go from a  few weeks to months on despite the risk  people continue to use this way to get  to Europe because so many have  successfully made it across while jiufen  JoJo's boat sank migrants on three other  vessels traveling with them made it to  the Canary Islands undetected by border  guards they send back pictures of  themselves from shopping malls or  standing next to expensive cars but they  don't show the hardship of life in  Europe  haunted by those who died despite the  failed attempt  Diouf is preparing to travel again it  appears his journey is not over  Nicholas Hawke al Jazeera bara Gambia
 

